{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-73940",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, multiplying each component of $v$ by $-3$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3v & =-3[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3v)\\cdot w & =12\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12-24+9-6-6 \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
